Rescoped for main (release 1.000). The replace rule from|to is documented as a regex since 1.000 (POD CONFIG FILE FORMAT, README, CLAUDE.md) - that stays, it is the contract now, not a bug.
The word rule is still broken: s/([^A-Za-z0-9]+)$from([^A-Za-z0-9]+)/$1$to$2/g needs a non-alphanumeric character on both sides and consumes them. Probe on main with hh%ah:
  "hh = 1;\nmy hh,hh\nend hh"  ->  "hh = 1;\nmy ah,hh\nend hh"
The word at the start of the text, the second of two adjacent words and the word at the end are all missed.
Work: match the word with lookaround against the alphanumeric class (start and end of text count as a boundary, the separators are not consumed), keep the documented meaning (hh does not match inside ohhh), keep $from as regex source like the replace rule. A test with exactly the probe text above.

